4  # PLAN.md stage this tree is graded against. Stage 5 (actors, runtime,
   # @meta) has not arrived, so tests carrying `.stage 5` are deferred.
   #
   # 4 IS THE GRADE, NOT A CLAIM THAT 1-4 ARE FINISHED.
   #
   # THE BOARD IS GREEN AND THAT IS NOW THE THING TO DISTRUST. As of
   # 2026-08-08 every suite passes -- 429 / 0, fixpoint byte-identical,
   # every scanner clean. Read that as "nothing we thought to check is
   # broken", never as "stage 4 is done", because the gap between those
   # two sentences is where every silent bug in this tree has lived.
   #
   # Measured, not asserted, and all of it below the grade:
   #
   #   - The LSP answers HOVER and nothing else. No diagnostics are ever
   #     published, and hover answers on an identifier's USE -- probing
   #     every identifier in a four-line function, 3 of 12 answered.
   #     Everything else is refused by name with -32601.
   #   - Stage 2's formatter models the FILE and not the DECLARATION. It
   #     normalises bytes, so `make fmt` is green; it does not know a
   #     declaration from a comment from a string literal.
   #   - Struct field defaults are specified twice in DESIGN.md and
   #     broken two ways. Nothing caught it because `src/` declares zero
   #     fields with defaults, so the compiler never eats the feature.
   #
   # That last one is the pattern, not an anecdote. A green suite
   # measures what the compiler uses on itself, and the differential
   # oracle is blind wherever both implementations are wrong the same
   # way. When auditing whether a doc is real, ask "does `src/` use
   # this?" -- not "does it build?".
   #
   # Lowering this number would defer the tests that are meant to fail
   # and make the board read better without a line of work being done,
   # which is the one thing it must not do.
